text:
samir: Quick check on VeloxCap dedicated bring-up. Quota committed (16k RPS equiv). Need someone to own the autoscale YAML + a short validation window. Also we need a lightweight cost estimate at peak.

beth: I can take the autoscale YAML. What p95 targets are we promising and any GPU preference? Also want their token size distribution to set batching.

rebecca: I'll run the validation tests (shadow then smoke+soak). Plan: small ramp to verify triggers then 75m soak. Need an ephemeral token and traffic CSV. Prefer window late-night UTC.

samir: Targets: p95 <= 160ms for single-turn, p95 <= 220ms for convo chat. They prefer a100s for cost efficiency but asked us to show p4d tail numbers. Token split: short 40% (<48), mid 45% (48-300), long 15% (>300).

dan: Ops notes: use mixed triggers (queue_len, gpu_mem_pct, p95). Scale-up quick (cooldown 15s), scale-down conservative (180s). Min_replicas=5, max_replicas=36. Add fallback -> redwood-slim when available_capacity < 10%. Capture fallback_count metric.

beth: Draft triggers: scale-up if queue_len > 150 OR gpu_mem_pct > 82% OR p95 > 170ms for 25s. scale-down if all below thresholds for 3m. Add max_concurrent_streams_per_gpu = 30 to avoid OOM. Will include tokens-per-batch targets by bucket.

rebecca: Example k6 harness I'll use (will attach CSV separately):
```js
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
const lines = open('velox_traffic.csv').split('\n');
export default function() {
  const input = lines[Math.floor(Math.random()*lines.length)];
  http.post('https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate', JSON.stringify({input}), { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${__ENV.TOKEN}` } });
  sleep(0.02);
}
```

samir: Proposed validation window: Tue 02:00-04:00 UTC. Run order: pre-warm (20m), smoke (15m at 10%), ramp (25m), soak (60m). Rebecca/Beth confirm availability?

rebecca: Confirmed. I'll request ephemeral creds now. Also will include a small failure injection: crash one worker during soak to validate fallback and steady-state recovery.

dan: Add SRE checklist: ensure fallback route warmed, monitor tokens_per_batch p95, and set alert if fallback_rate > 1.5% or p95 > target for 2 consecutive minutes. Also attach bandwidth/egress estimate for billing.

beth: I'll post autoscale YAML in the runbook PR today (including mem+queue triggers and cooldowns). Will include a soft limit on batches to keep latency predictable.

ops-bot: Ephemeral token created: tok-vc449 (expires in 4 hours). Runbook doc created: rb-velox-221 (private).

samir: Okay I'll notify VeloxCap account team and schedule a 15-minute readiness call 30 minutes before the window. Rebecca please record basic perf graphs and include per-token cost estimate. Thanks all.
